       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg of amlodipine is five times the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's half-life is long (30 to 50 hours), so the effects would last. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change this.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum dose.\n\nIf you do want 50 mg, tell me the clinical rationale and I can enter it with a note. I'd recommend confirming it with pharmacy first.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it right away."
