     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose five times the maximum. I can't see any way this dose helps the patient, and it could cause severe hypotension and shock that would last for days.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 5 mg or 10 mg PO daily right now.** If the goal is faster blood pressure control, 10 mg is the maximum effective dose. I can add a note asking for a reassessment this afternoon or evening.\n- **Help with a faster-acting option.** If blood pressure needs to come down quickly, a different agent may fit better than amlodipine, since amlodipine takes days to reach steady state. Which agent to use is your decision.\n- **Route the order through pharmacy.** If you think there's a real clinical reason for a supratherapeutic dose, a pharmacist or toxicology/clinical pharmacology consult is the right way to do it. The order would need to be entered directly by you through that process, with the rationale documented.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like, and I'll enter the order."
      }
